The description is too sparse to classify with confidence: it says only that the sleeves and hem bottom have raw, unfinished edges. That points to a garment with sleeves, most likely a top such as a T-shirt or sweatshirt. Fiber content and knit versus woven construction are not given. The most common garment with raw-edge sleeves and hem is a knit cotton top, so I chose cotton knit T-shirts as the best guess.

HTSUS 6109.10.0012 is the number I recall for women's cotton T-shirts, but I am not certain of the statistical suffix. The 6109.10.00 subheading covers T-shirts, singlets, tank tops and similar garments, knitted or crocheted, of cotton. The suffixes I recall are 6109.10.0004 (men's, cotton, "Men's or boys'"), 6109.10.0012 (women's or girls'), and 6109.10.0018 (other). I am going with 6109.10.0012.

